{"id": "EUVD-2026-108676", "enisaUuid": "a68b5725-358a-30da-b101-580de287c18a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Add range checks for dec_output_info\n\nIf the driver's dec_output_info contains invalid data the driver can\nwrite in invalid memory. Add a range check for that.\n\nThis fixes this smatch error:\ndrivers/media/platform/chips-media/wave5/wave5-vpuapi.c:588 wave5_vpu_dec_get_output_info() error: buffer overflow 'inst->frame_buf' 64 <= 127", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d6f777d11c7b34549cdadd8578d4b85f685eb976", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/144f24ec0fc1e51673611912a6d14ded0a61db43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79aef69bb0903616f4867f0168aea717a11c439c", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98882"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fg2v-3chx-7cvc", "CVE-2026-98882"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1bf63da1-2d6b-3665-92b6-2a4b92b777c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "4537391b-13fb-3717-94d6-c0bb60c2a63e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "473916b6-df5d-32d5-b7a4-75e1a94e65a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.53"}, {"id": "5f89ccf5-4d21-32fb-b67a-f4760a246e88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "84d68c6a-9160-3d49-81c7-6de984d2d851", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <144f24ec0fc1e51673611912a6d14ded0a61db43"}, {"id": "92bfb34c-1279-3e71-ad35-2083be37c58c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <79aef69bb0903616